mh2lm: isolate PON PMIC-arb route reads (0130)

The 0114a2 key diagnostic established a precise boundary: the same kernel
reaches iOS with sweetkeysirqdiag=1 (SPMI helper only), but
sweetkeysirqdiag=2 returns to the LG BSP while querying PON's complete route.
The successful init log proves the normal key driver has already found PON at
APID 248 and can poll it. Existing battery route logs prove the generic
PMIC-arb v5 diagnostic accesses work for APIDs 266 and 269. The remaining
unproven accesses are PON-specific IRQ-route registers.

Split a route diagnostic into independent read-only parts: APID metadata,
the intr-region owner bitmap, the PON channel ACC_ENABLE word, and its
IRQ_STATUS word. The legacy full route API continues to run all parts. New
key masks 0x20/0x40/0x80/0x100 run only one PON part each after the helper is
initialized. Nothing registers the GIC SPI, writes PDC, enables/clears PMIC
interrupts, or changes the polling fallback.

